675
00:33:16,316 --> 00:33:16,876
[SPEAKER_00]: Curveball.

676
00:33:17,036 --> 00:33:18,837
[SPEAKER_00]: I was about to throw a curveball.

677
00:33:19,097 --> 00:33:19,597
[SPEAKER_00]: It didn't hurt.

678
00:33:19,617 --> 00:33:21,158
[SPEAKER_01]: He signaled you to throw the curve?

679
00:33:21,198 --> 00:33:21,538
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

680
00:33:21,878 --> 00:33:23,099
[SPEAKER_00]: He signaled the coach?

681
00:33:23,259 --> 00:33:24,819
[SPEAKER_00]: The coach signaled Jimmy Dykes.

682
00:33:26,160 --> 00:33:29,721
[SPEAKER_00]: He was coaching more of the athletics.

683
00:33:30,262 --> 00:33:31,282
[SPEAKER_00]: And he had tipped him off.

684
00:33:31,322 --> 00:33:32,102
[SPEAKER_00]: I found that out later.

685
00:33:32,122 --> 00:33:33,723
[SPEAKER_00]: He tipped him off with a curveball.

686
00:33:34,500 --> 00:33:35,981
[SPEAKER_00]: Probably got a flash from the catcher.

687
00:33:37,842 --> 00:33:38,723
[SPEAKER_00]: But it didn't curve.

688
00:33:39,023 --> 00:33:41,104
[SPEAKER_00]: He stepped into it and hit him right in the back of the ear.

689
00:33:41,785 --> 00:33:46,408
[SPEAKER_00]: And he just went over like that.

690
00:33:46,548 --> 00:33:48,389
[SPEAKER_00]: Blood coming out of his nose.

691
00:33:48,429 --> 00:33:50,790
[SPEAKER_00]: Boy, that scared the heck out of me.

692
00:33:50,830 --> 00:33:51,611
[SPEAKER_00]: I didn't want to hit him.

693
00:33:51,671 --> 00:33:52,691
[SPEAKER_00]: I wanted to brush him back.

694
00:33:52,711 --> 00:33:53,692
[SPEAKER_00]: But he stepped into it.

695
00:33:54,953 --> 00:33:56,554
[SPEAKER_00]: Like a curveball, he stepped into it.

696
00:33:57,474 --> 00:33:59,876
[SPEAKER_00]: But he stepped into a fast one, and that was pretty fast.

697
00:34:03,850 --> 00:34:06,412
[SPEAKER_01]: Did that upset you for pitching after that?

698
00:34:06,532 --> 00:34:06,733
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

699
00:34:06,773 --> 00:34:11,777
[SPEAKER_00]: The cop erased him because I hit him in the head with a duster.

700
00:34:11,797 --> 00:34:12,958
[SPEAKER_00]: What was I going to do?

701
00:34:14,159 --> 00:34:20,825
[SPEAKER_00]: The only fine I ever got in my life was $10 from him for not coming close enough to a hitter.

702
00:34:22,106 --> 00:34:24,769
[SPEAKER_00]: $10 for all the years I played ball.

703
00:34:24,789 --> 00:34:25,890
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the only time I ever got.

704
00:34:27,551 --> 00:34:28,592
[SPEAKER_01]: And it made it stick, too.

705
00:34:31,250 --> 00:34:34,831
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, did he come in from center field much and consult with you?

706
00:34:34,931 --> 00:34:35,171
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

707
00:34:35,331 --> 00:34:36,611
[SPEAKER_00]: Not too, no.

708
00:34:36,651 --> 00:34:39,952
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how you manage from way out in center field.

709
00:34:39,972 --> 00:34:42,612
[SPEAKER_00]: It's kind of tricky.

710
00:34:42,632 --> 00:34:43,532
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, he'd look around.

711
00:34:43,572 --> 00:34:44,173
[SPEAKER_00]: He'd look around.

712
00:34:44,193 --> 00:34:47,393
[SPEAKER_01]: He had a knockdown sign or something like that.

713
00:34:47,413 --> 00:34:49,694
[SPEAKER_01]: He'd reach down and get a plate of grass and put it in his mouth.

714
00:34:50,214 --> 00:34:52,054
[SPEAKER_00]: I'd have to turn around and look and see him do that.

715
00:34:52,914 --> 00:34:54,374
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure enough, here's Bassler with a...

716
00:34:56,115 --> 00:34:56,415
[SPEAKER_01]: I see.

717
00:35:02,679 --> 00:35:11,741
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, the boy was looking last night to get a picture of the 1926 Carlo team.

718
00:35:11,781 --> 00:35:20,723
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I was just looking for a picture of the 1926 team.

719
00:35:21,203 --> 00:35:22,283
[SPEAKER_01]: Jess Haines.

720
00:35:22,603 --> 00:35:24,603
[SPEAKER_01]: Jess Haines doesn't live far from us.

721
00:35:24,683 --> 00:35:25,844
[SPEAKER_01]: We were over visiting him.

722
00:35:26,664 --> 00:35:29,985
[SPEAKER_01]: He's got a couple of those big team pictures up in his little den there.

723
00:35:30,005 --> 00:35:31,905
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, he's got the same one of the 1926 team.

724
00:35:33,243 --> 00:35:37,486
[SPEAKER_00]: 31, then 30, 28.

725
00:35:37,546 --> 00:35:42,250
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, 26 was the big one for Jess, too.

726
00:35:43,571 --> 00:35:46,513
[SPEAKER_00]: He pitched against the Yankees in that series.

727
00:35:47,293 --> 00:35:50,396
[SPEAKER_00]: They say his damn knuckles were bleeding, you know.

728
00:35:50,436 --> 00:35:52,417
[SPEAKER_00]: But a knuckleball pitcher, Jess was, too.

729
00:35:55,940 --> 00:35:57,741
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you get to know Alexander very well?

730
00:35:57,841 --> 00:35:58,502
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah.

731
00:36:01,627 --> 00:36:04,649
[SPEAKER_01]: Did he take such poor care of himself, as they say?

732
00:36:06,229 --> 00:36:18,156
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, a lot of times, you know, you pick up the paper, you see that they find Alexander in the gutter or some darn place, you know.

733
00:36:19,096 --> 00:36:20,497
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, he's subject to epileptic.

734
00:36:22,498 --> 00:36:26,440
[SPEAKER_00]: See, you get one of these damn fits, and away he goes.

735
00:36:26,500 --> 00:36:30,182
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course, Alex would drink, too, but most of the time,

736
00:36:30,989 --> 00:36:34,231
[SPEAKER_00]: I remember one time in Cincinnati, we were getting ready to go to the ballpark.

737
00:36:35,692 --> 00:36:37,013
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where the car goes.

738
00:36:37,513 --> 00:36:40,735
[SPEAKER_00]: And he had his straw hats on, you know.

739
00:36:40,755 --> 00:36:45,558
[SPEAKER_00]: We were sitting in the lobby there, sitting in the hotel.

740
00:36:45,618 --> 00:36:46,879
[SPEAKER_00]: All of a sudden, Pete gets up.

741
00:36:48,140 --> 00:36:50,601
[SPEAKER_00]: And he just stares around, and down he goes.

742
00:36:51,522 --> 00:36:53,483
[SPEAKER_00]: So we all run over and got a hold of him.

743
00:36:54,784 --> 00:36:56,785
[SPEAKER_00]: So he come in one of those epileptics.

744
00:36:57,445 --> 00:36:59,887
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he come in and got in the

745
00:37:01,277 --> 00:37:15,288
[SPEAKER_00]: Then I went up in Philadelphia, got into one of those downy goes, and a whole ball club went around, circled around him.

746
00:37:16,309 --> 00:37:24,836
