00:39:11,576 --> 00:39:13,657
[SPEAKER_01]: Are there those you can work better with than others?

778
00:39:13,757 --> 00:39:16,339
[SPEAKER_00]: I work good with Jimmy, Jimmy Wilson.

779
00:39:18,441 --> 00:39:23,625
[SPEAKER_01]: You learn to understand each other, what's the best pitches?

780
00:39:24,964 --> 00:39:26,365
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you ever shake him off much?

781
00:39:26,725 --> 00:39:27,346
[SPEAKER_00]: Not too much.

782
00:39:27,926 --> 00:39:32,889
[SPEAKER_00]: I'd shake off him, but I'd come right back the same way.

783
00:39:33,870 --> 00:39:37,372
[SPEAKER_00]: You might give me a curveball, and I'd raise your nose like that, and come right back with a curve.

784
00:39:37,632 --> 00:39:38,493
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I see.

785
00:39:38,993 --> 00:39:39,573
[SPEAKER_00]: Pretty tricky.

786
00:39:39,873 --> 00:39:46,578
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you're hitting up there, just for a second, you might wonder, what the hell is he going to throw me?

787
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:50,820
[SPEAKER_01]: How was your spitball?

788
00:39:51,541 --> 00:39:51,841
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

789
00:39:52,161 --> 00:39:54,643
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I can throw at every ball.

790
00:39:55,328 --> 00:39:55,648
[SPEAKER_00]: Did you?

791
00:39:56,169 --> 00:39:58,010
[SPEAKER_00]: I could, I say, because it was outlawed.

792
00:39:58,190 --> 00:39:58,791
[SPEAKER_00]: I know it was.

793
00:40:00,252 --> 00:40:11,622
[SPEAKER_00]: You see, when we left Portland in 1921, Walter McQueen, he registered all of us, spitballs, spitballs.

794
00:40:13,183 --> 00:40:14,324
[SPEAKER_00]: So we were eligible then.

795
00:40:15,385 --> 00:40:16,666
[SPEAKER_01]: Even though you'd been in the minors?

796
00:40:17,306 --> 00:40:21,050
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I don't know about the major leagues, but we were eligible in the Coast League.

797
00:40:21,130 --> 00:40:21,470
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, I see.

798
00:40:23,203 --> 00:40:29,725
[SPEAKER_00]: But they had spitballers up there, Shocker, and Iron Spitzel, and who was the great one over?

799
00:40:29,765 --> 00:40:30,526
[SPEAKER_00]: Burleigh Grimes.

800
00:40:30,546 --> 00:40:31,526
[SPEAKER_00]: Burleigh Grimes.

801
00:40:31,546 --> 00:40:32,206
[SPEAKER_01]: Kovaleski.

802
00:40:32,546 --> 00:40:34,447
[SPEAKER_00]: Kovaleski and who was it?

803
00:40:34,467 --> 00:40:35,327
[SPEAKER_01]: Jack Quinn.

804
00:40:35,427 --> 00:40:35,968
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

805
00:40:36,328 --> 00:40:37,908
[SPEAKER_00]: There were quite a few of them.

806
00:40:38,969 --> 00:40:45,871
[SPEAKER_00]: And they had quite a few of them that could throw that good little rough spot on the ball, you know, and do tricks with it.

807
00:40:46,411 --> 00:40:48,472
[SPEAKER_01]: You said you could throw the Emory ball.

