[SPEAKER_00]: Towards the last, I'd throw a few screwballs, too, you know, to get her with my fastball.

820
00:41:57,148 --> 00:41:58,710
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the reverse curve?

821
00:41:58,730 --> 00:41:59,450
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, reverse, too.

822
00:41:59,851 --> 00:42:01,752
[SPEAKER_01]: Isn't that kind of hard on your elbow or something?

823
00:42:02,293 --> 00:42:02,653
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

824
00:42:02,833 --> 00:42:03,794
[SPEAKER_00]: Not a natural.

825
00:42:03,874 --> 00:42:06,657
[SPEAKER_00]: You see, there's a certain way you can hold that ball and make it dip, too.

826
00:42:08,318 --> 00:42:11,121
[SPEAKER_00]: If you hold it cross-seam, that's the way it is.

827
00:42:11,141 --> 00:42:16,225
[SPEAKER_00]: See, I'd hold it wide cross-seam and go like that in the bowl and catch these four seams going around.

828
00:42:16,245 --> 00:42:18,167
[SPEAKER_00]: A lot of spin on it, see, and it'd take off a little.

829
00:42:19,320 --> 00:42:25,344
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you throw it this way with just a little dip and hold on to the end of the seam, it's following two seams.

830
00:42:26,385 --> 00:42:28,386
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't get that resistance, so you dip.

831
00:42:30,308 --> 00:42:31,188
[SPEAKER_00]: You get a dip on it.

832
00:42:34,751 --> 00:42:40,035
[SPEAKER_00]: I used to throw a lot of that to Mel Ott with the Giants.

833
00:42:41,996 --> 00:42:42,877
[SPEAKER_01]: He was a tough one.

834
00:42:43,117 --> 00:42:43,477
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah.

